1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,140
This con man supposedly sold the fucking Eiffel Tower.

2
00:00:03,780 --> 00:00:07,400
His name's Victor Lustig, and yeah, he called himself a count.

3
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:10,460
That's a noble title, but his came from nowhere.

4
00:00:11,180 --> 00:00:14,020
So here's the legend. Paris, nineteen twenty-five.

5
00:00:14,900 --> 00:00:17,700
He pretends to work for the government, and books a fancy hotel.

6
00:00:18,300 --> 00:00:22,360
Then five scrap-metal dealers show up, guys who buy old metal to melt down.

7
00:00:22,780 --> 00:00:26,340
And he tells them, keep it quiet, the tower's being sold for scrap.

8
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:28,820
Double-tap if you'd have laughed him out of the room.

9
00:00:28,820 --> 00:00:33,000
One dealer, Poisson, reportedly paid. And Lustig was gone.

10
00:00:33,620 --> 00:00:36,900
The best part? Poisson was too damn embarrassed to call the police.

11
00:00:37,720 --> 00:00:41,040
So then, legend says, Lustig came back and ran it again.

12
00:00:41,600 --> 00:00:44,320
But none of that was ever proven in court. Zero.

13
00:00:44,860 --> 00:00:47,280
Send this to the friend who'd fall for this, no question.

14
00:00:47,860 --> 00:00:50,060
What's proven? He got into counterfeiting.

15
00:00:50,360 --> 00:00:53,060
That means making fake money, then passing it off as real.

16
00:00:53,600 --> 00:00:57,280
He even reportedly sold a box that supposedly printed hundred-dollar bills.

17
00:00:57,800 --> 00:01:01,660
In May nineteen thirty-five, the Secret Service arrested him in New York.

18
00:01:02,200 --> 00:01:03,980
That's the agency that chases fake cash.

19
00:01:04,760 --> 00:01:08,700
Then this guy escaped from a federal jail. Like, actually escaped.

20
00:01:09,320 --> 00:01:11,040
Weeks later, they caught his ass again.

21
00:01:11,620 --> 00:01:14,100
Follow, 'cause here's what twenty years looks like.

22
00:01:14,460 --> 00:01:19,320
He pleaded guilty. Fifteen years for the fake money, and five for the escape.

23
00:01:19,340 --> 00:01:22,800
Twenty years, at Alcatraz, the island prison in San Francisco Bay.

24
00:01:23,260 --> 00:01:27,580
And he was never even charged for the Eiffel Tower. The fake cash is what got him.

25
00:01:28,040 --> 00:01:30,560
Real con or bullshit legend? One word.

